# Help articles with product changes

Skill: [help-articles](../skills/help-articles/SKILL.md). Support layout: [support-project.mdc](support-project.mdc).

A **user-visible** WebOnOne change is not done until Support Markdown matches it (`support/frontend/src/content/en` and `si`).

## Document

New/renamed nav or page, new user workflow, role-gated UI, meaning of money or charts, removed/moved screens.

## Skip

Internal APIs, migrations, Redux, tests, i18n-only, bug fixes with no usage change, deploy/dev ops.

## Same task

Product agent may only edit its service root. It **must** return `Support docs: required | not needed` with slug and bullets when required. Parent or **support-agent** writes the articles before the task is closed. Do not store articles in MySQL. Do not put `npm run dev` or IIS in public articles.

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w support-root
```

Manual: `http://127.0.0.1:3021/docs/{category}/{slug}`.
